title: La ciudad
max-visits: 1
view-if: 0
# Container/namespace only — NOT tagged event. The urban track (banda="ciudad"): the Liga
# Comunista 23 de Septiembre in Guadalajara, on Guillén's doctrine. A decentralized network of
# cells (u_celulas). You act loud (expropiaciones, propaganda armada) and survive the Brigada
# Blanca (u_calor + the cascade) by decentralization, toward ingobernabilidad (u_poder).
# apoyo_popular is the urban sympathy. u_seguridad is compartmentalization.

# =====================================================================
# PHASE 0 — LA RED. How you build the network. Guillén: the city is the terrain; decentralize.
# =====================================================================
@forjar
title: Tejer la red
new-page: true
face-image: img/guillen.jpg
subtitle: "Concrete forests are safer than forests of trees" — Abraham Guillén
on-arrival: u_phase = "forjar"

= Tejer la red

Guillén said it against Che himself: in a country that is already more city than country, the sierra is a detour and the *metropolis* is the terrain. Concrete forests are safer than forests of trees; the city has more people to hide in, more banks to fund the war, more targets that matter. But the city is also the state's ground — its files, its informers, its Brigada Blanca forming this very year under the DFS — and the only thing that lets a network survive there is the thing Guillén hammered on and the foco never learned: *decentralization.* No single head to cut off. No column to encircle. Cells that do not know each other. How you weave the first threads decides whether the net catches the state or the state catches you.

- @forjar_estudiantes: **Desde la universidad.** Build from the student movement — the FER, the prepas, the radicalized campuses where the Liga was actually born. *(fast growth, deep sympathy; the campuses are watched)*
- @forjar_obreros: **Desde la fábrica.** Root the network in the industrial belt — slower, harder to grow, far harder to kill. *(rooted, resilient cells; less spectacular)*
- @forjar_clandestino: **La compartimentación.** Build small and dark from the start — Guillén's rule, cells sealed from each other, growth traded for security. *(fewer cells, high compartmentalization)*

@forjar_estudiantes
on-arrival: {! Q.u_entreno="estudiantes"; Q.u_forjado=1; Q.u_phase="red"; Q.u_celulas+=2; Q.apoyo_popular+=8; Q.u_calor+=8; Q.sup_students=(Q.sup_students||0)+6; !}

You build where the Liga really began — the University of Guadalajara, the FER, the prepas full of students who have read Guillén and Marighella and decided that the time for marching is over. The network grows fast; a campus radicalizes in weeks, not years, and the sympathy runs deep among the young. It also grows *visible* — the DFS has an informer in every faculty, and a movement built from students is a movement whose faces are already in a file somewhere. Fast, and warm, and watched.

- @root: A la calle. Continuar.

@forjar_obreros
on-arrival: {! Q.u_entreno="obreros"; Q.u_forjado=1; Q.u_phase="red"; Q.u_celulas+=1; Q.u_seguridad+=8; Q.sup_workers=(Q.sup_workers||0)+5; Q.apoyo_popular+=4; !}

You do the harder, slower thing and root the network in the working class — the industrial colonias, the factory gates, the men and women who cannot afford romanticism and will not join for a season. It grows at a crawl. It is also nearly impossible to kill: a cell embedded in a working-class barrio that has known its members since childhood does not fall to an informer the way a campus does, because there are no strangers to inform. Fewer, slower, and rooted in ground the Brigada Blanca cannot simply walk into.

- @root: A la calle. Continuar.

@forjar_clandestino
on-arrival: {! Q.u_entreno="clandestino"; Q.u_forjado=1; Q.u_phase="red"; Q.u_seguridad+=16; Q.inteligencia+=4; Q.apoyo_popular-=2; !}

You follow Guillén to the letter: no mass base to be rounded up, no campus cells that all know each other, just a handful of sealed compartments that could each be destroyed without touching the next. It is the most survivable way to begin and the loneliest — you trade the warmth and the numbers of a movement for the cold arithmetic of survival, betting that a network the state cannot map is worth more than one it cannot ignore. Small. Dark. Very hard to kill.

- @root: A la calle. Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# PHASE 1 — LA RED EN ACCIÓN. The "La red" card each month: grow, expropriate, propagandize, or lie low.
# =====================================================================
@red
title: La red
card-image: img/la liga.webp
subtitle: Guadalajara — the cells, the money, the heat
view-if: banda = "ciudad" and u_forjado = 1 and u_phase = "red"
is-card: true
frequency: 100
max-visits: 300
tags: lared

= La red en acción

The network: **[+ u_celulas +]** cells · seguridad **[+ u_seguridad : entero +]**/100 · simpatía (el agua) **[+ apoyo_popular : entero +]**/100 · fondos **[+ funds : entero +]** · parque **[+ parque : entero +]**. The Brigada Blanca's heat: **[+ u_calor : entero +]**/100. Poder popular: **[+ u_poder : entero +]**/100. **Puntos de acción: [+ acc_pts +]/[+ acc_max +].** [? if u_calor >= 70 : *The white brigade is close — a raid is coming. Lie low, or accept the risk.* ?][? if u_celulas <= 1 : *The network is nearly gone.* ?][? if acc_pts <= 0 : *No points left — end the month.* ?]

Las órdenes de la dirección — el mando se abre en tres:

- @cat_accion: **Acción armada.** Expropiaciones, armerías, la acción directa que financia y arma la red.
- @cat_propaganda: **Propaganda y comunicaciones.** Radio, colonias tomadas, comunicados — hacer visible al movimiento.
- @cat_red: **La red y la seguridad.** Tejer células, compartimentar, casas de seguridad, bajar el calor.
- @return: **Volver.** Guardar la carta y elegir otra cosa este mes.
- @fin_mes: **Terminar el mes.** Pasar al siguiente; los puntos se reponen.

@cat_accion
new-page: true
title: Acción armada
subtitle: Autofinanciamiento — la ciudad paga la guerra
face-image: img/bankrobbery.jpg

= Acción armada

Células **[+ u_celulas +]** · fondos **[+ funds : entero +]** · parque **[+ parque : entero +]** · seguridad **[+ u_seguridad : entero +]** · calor **[+ u_calor : entero +]**/100. **Puntos: [+ acc_pts +]/[+ acc_max +]**. Guillén: the city has the banks, the payrolls, the armouries — a network that cannot pay itself cannot last a month.

- @r_expro: **Expropiación.** A bank or payroll — take the war chest from the enemy's own vaults. *(2 pts; +fondos, +parque, +heat)*
- @a_armeria: **Asalto a una armería.** Guns, not money — arm the cells directly. *(2 pts; +parque; heavy heat)*
- @a_ajuste: **Ajuste de cuentas.** Strike a torturer or a strike-breaking boss the barrios already hate. *(2 pts; +poder popular; hard heat, and a line crossed)*
- @red: Volver al mando.

@cat_propaganda
new-page: true
title: Propaganda y comunicaciones
subtitle: Hacer visible al movimiento — y hablarle a la ciudad
face-image: img/radio_ayuntamiento.jpg

= Propaganda y comunicaciones

Simpatía (el agua) **[+ apoyo_popular : entero +]**/100 · poder popular **[+ u_poder : entero +]**/100 · calor **[+ u_calor : entero +]**/100. **Puntos: [+ acc_pts +]/[+ acc_max +]**. The Tupamaro insight: an action nobody hears about is only a robbery. The communiqué *is* the weapon.

- @r_propaganda: **Propaganda armada.** Seize a radio station and read the communiqué into a hundred thousand kitchens. *(2 pts; +simpatía, +poder, +heat)*
- @p_colonia: **Toma de una colonia.** The Pando model — occupy a barrio for an hour, address it, hand out food and manifestos, withdraw before the army arrives. *(2 pts; big +poder +simpatía; big heat)*
- @p_prensa: **Comunicado a la prensa.** Get the movement's word past the censor into a national daily. *(1 pt; −legitimidad del régimen; +heat)*
- @p_pinta: **Pintas y volantes.** The unglamorous work — walls, leaflets, the night shift. *(1 pt; small +simpatía; almost no heat)*
- @red: Volver al mando.

@cat_red
new-page: true
title: La red y la seguridad
subtitle: Compartimentar — la única armadura del guerrillero urbano
face-image: img/safehouse.jpg

= La red y la seguridad

Células **[+ u_celulas +]** · seguridad **[+ u_seguridad : entero +]**/100 · calor **[+ u_calor : entero +]**/100. **Puntos: [+ acc_pts +]/[+ acc_max +]**. [? if u_calor >= 70 : *The white brigade is close — go quiet.* ?] Guillén's rule: no single head to cut off. What the state cannot map, it cannot roll up.

- @r_celula: **Tejer una célula.** Recruit and seal a new cell into the net. *(1 pt; +células, a little heat)*
- @s_compartimentar: **Compartimentar.** Re-seal the compartments — nobody knows more than they must. *(1 pt; +seguridad; the cascade stops at one door)*
- @s_casa: **Casa de seguridad.** Open a new safehouse and rotate the burned ones. *(1 pt; +seguridad, −heat; costs fondos)*
- @r_bajar: **Bajar la actividad.** Go dormant while the heat cools. *(1 pt; −heat, +seguridad)*
- @red: Volver al mando.

@r_celula
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.u_celulas+=1; Q.u_calor+=4; if(Q.u_entreno==="clandestino"){Q.u_seguridad+=2;} Q.apoyo_popular+=2; !}

You weave another cell into the net — new people, sealed off from the ones who recruited them, taught the discipline of knowing only what they must. The network grows a little wider and a little harder to unravel, because every cell that does not know its neighbors is a thread the Brigada Blanca can pull without the whole thing coming apart. A movement is being built in the concrete forest, quietly, one sealed room at a time.

- @red: Continuar.

@r_expro
face-image: img/bankrobbery.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 2 and u_celulas >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: An expropriation costs 2 action points and at least two cells working in concert.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=2; var _r=(Q.u_celulas*8)+(Q.u_seguridad*0.3)-30+(Math.random()*35-12); if(_r>=0){Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)+16;Q.parque=(Q.parque||0)+8;Q.u_poder+=2;}else{Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)+6;Q.u_celulas-=1;Q.u_calor+=10;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+1;} Q.u_calor+=14; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+2; !}

You do what Guillén said the city offers and the sierra never will: you take your war chest from the enemy's own banks. [? if u_seguridad >= 50 : It goes clean — the cell is in and out in ninety seconds, the money funds a year of clandestine life, the guns for it bought with the bourgeoisie's own deposits. ?][? if u_seguridad < 50 : It goes loud — a getaway that nearly wasn't, a cell burned in the doing, a face on a security photograph. You got the money. It cost you.  ?] Every peso raises the war chest and the heat in the same motion: a bank robbery is a flare that says *we are here,* and the Brigada Blanca reads flares.

- @red: Continuar.

@r_propaganda
face-image: img/radio_ayuntamiento.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Armed propaganda costs 2 action points.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=2; Q.apoyo_popular+=8; Q.u_poder+=6; Q.u_calor+=12; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} Q.legitimidad_regimen-=2; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+2; Q.u_pando=(Q.u_pando||0)+1; !}

You do the thing the Tupamaros made famous: you make the movement *visible* on your own terms. A radio station seized for ten minutes and a communiqué read into a hundred thousand kitchens; or a colonia taken for an hour — the Pando model — occupied, addressed, given food and manifestos, and abandoned before the army can arrive. The city learns that there is a power in it that the state cannot see and cannot stop, and the poder popular — the sense that another authority exists — climbs. So does the heat: nothing focuses the Brigada Blanca like being publicly humiliated.

- @red: Continuar.

@r_bajar
face-image: img/safehouse.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.u_calor-=22; if(Q.u_calor<0){Q.u_calor=0;} Q.u_seguridad+=6; if(Q.u_seguridad>100){Q.u_seguridad=100;} !}

You call everything off. The cells go dark — no operations, no meetings that can be traced, the safehouses rotated, the compartments re-sealed, the network doing the patient, invisible, unglamorous work of simply *surviving* while the white brigade's heat cools for lack of anything to chase. It is the discipline that separates a network that lasts from a foco that flares and dies: knowing when the loudest and bravest thing to do is nothing at all. The heat drops. The war waits.

- @red: Continuar.

@fin_mes
new-page: true
on-arrival: month_actions = 1
go-to: root

@a_armeria
face-image: img/bankrobbery.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 2 and u_celulas >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: An armoury raid costs 2 action points and at least two cells.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=2; var _r=(Q.u_celulas*7)+(Q.u_seguridad*0.3)-34+(Math.random()*34-12); if(_r>=0){Q.parque=(Q.parque||0)+18;Q.u_poder+=2;}else{Q.parque=(Q.parque||0)+5;Q.u_celulas-=1;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+1;} Q.u_calor+=18; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+3; !}

You go for the guns themselves — a police armoury, a factory's security lockup, a rural guard post on the edge of the city. [? if u_seguridad >= 50 : It is over in three minutes and the cells come out carrying more firepower than a year of expropriations could buy. ?][? if u_seguridad < 50 : It turns into a firefight in a corridor, and you come out with crates and one fewer compañero. ?] Weapons are worth more than money to a network that already has money, and nothing enrages a state like being disarmed by the people it disarmed.

- @red: Continuar.

@a_ajuste
choose-if: acc_pts >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: An ajusticiamiento costs 2 action points.
on-arrival: {! Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+2; Q.acc_pts-=2; Q.u_poder+=7; Q.apoyo_popular+=3; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=3; Q.u_calor+=22; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+4; Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; !}

You strike a man the barrios already curse by name — a torturer from the DFS, a boss who has strikers shot, a judge who signs whatever the palace sends him. In the colonias it lands like justice arriving for the first time in living memory, and the poder popular jumps: there is a power in this city that answers for the poor. It also crosses the line the state has been waiting for you to cross, and now the hunt is personal, and total. Every movement that did this learned that the applause fades faster than the manhunt.

- @red: Continuar.

@p_colonia
face-image: img/guadalajara1970s.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 2 and u_celulas >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: Taking a colonia costs 2 action points and at least three cells.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=2; Q.apoyo_popular+=12; Q.u_poder+=10; Q.u_calor+=18; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} Q.legitimidad_regimen-=4; Q.u_pando=(Q.u_pando||0)+1; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)-4; if(Q.funds<0){Q.funds=0;} !}

You do the thing the Tupamaros did at Pando and everyone remembered: for one hour, a whole barrio belongs to the movement. The cells take the streets, the phone line, the market; the militants speak from a truck bed; expropriated food goes out door to door with the manifesto; and then, before the army's trucks can reach the edge of the colonia, you are gone. It is not a battle — it is a *demonstration*, and what it demonstrates is that the state's monopoly on the city is a polite fiction. The barrio remembers it for a generation.

- @red: Continuar.

@p_prensa
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=5; Q.apoyo_popular+=3; Q.u_calor+=6; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} Q.escandalos=(Q.escandalos||0)+1; !}

You get the word past the censor: a manifesto printed, a disappearance documented, the names of the tortured set in type where the whole country reads them over breakfast. It costs the regime the one thing it guards more jealously than any garrison — the story it tells about itself. A dirty war depends on nobody being able to prove it is happening.

- @red: Continuar.

@p_pinta
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.apoyo_popular+=4; Q.u_poder+=2; Q.u_calor+=2; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} !}

The night shift: paint on walls, leaflets under doors, the movement's initials on every third corner by morning. It is the least glamorous work in the repertoire and the most patient — the slow accumulation of a presence, so that when the big actions come the city already knows the name behind them. Cheap, quiet, and it builds the water an inch at a time.

- @red: Continuar.

@s_compartimentar
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.u_seguridad+=12; if(Q.u_seguridad>100){Q.u_seguridad=100;} Q.u_calor-=4; if(Q.u_calor<0){Q.u_calor=0;} !}

You spend the month doing what Guillén said matters more than any operation: re-sealing the compartments. Contacts rebuilt through cut-outs, meeting protocols changed, the roster of who-knows-what pruned until no captured comrade could bring down more than his own cell. It is invisible, tedious, and it is the single reason some networks survived the Brigada Blanca and others became a list of names read out in a police station.

- @red: Continuar.

@s_casa
face-image: img/safehouse.jpg
choose-if: acc_pts >= 1 and funds >= 6
unavailable-subtitle: A new safehouse costs 1 action point and 6 fondos.
on-arrival: {! Q.acc_pts-=1; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)-6; Q.u_seguridad+=8; if(Q.u_seguridad>100){Q.u_seguridad=100;} Q.u_calor-=8; if(Q.u_calor<0){Q.u_calor=0;} !}

A rented room under a false name in a colonia where nobody asks; the burned houses abandoned, the compromised ones emptied before the knock comes. A network lives or dies on the addresses the state does not have, and rotating them is the rent you pay for staying alive in a city that is entirely the enemy's ground.

- @red: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# LA REDADA — the Brigada Blanca raid. Fires when the heat is high. A cell falls; it can cascade.
# =====================================================================
@redada
title: La redada
new-page: true
face-image: img/nightraid.webp
subtitle: The Brigada Blanca hits a safehouse — and pulls the thread
tags: event
view-if: banda = "ciudad" and u_phase = "red" and u_calor >= 70 and time >= u_redada_last + 2
priority: 9
frequency: 100
max-visits: 30
on-arrival: u_redada_last = time

= La redada

It comes the way it always came for the Liga: at four in the morning, at a safehouse, with the Brigada Blanca — the DFS's white brigade, off the books and above the law — coming through the door before anyone reaches a weapon. A cell is taken. And now the whole network holds its breath, because everything depends on the one thing you built or failed to build: compartmentalization. If the cells were sealed, the damage stops at one door. If they were not — if the taken comrades know names, addresses, the next safehouse — then the raid does not end here. It *cascades*, one interrogation at a time, exactly the way the real Liga was rolled up, cell pulling cell until there is nothing left to pull.

- @rd_aguantar: **Aguantar.** Trust the compartments and the comrades' silence — the cell is lost, but the seals hold and the network survives. *(needs security; the cascade stops at one door)*
- @rd_disolver: **Disolver y dispersar.** Assume the worst — scatter the network, abandon the safehouses, go completely dark before the thread unravels. *(lose cells + poder, but kill the cascade and cut the heat)*
- @rd_responder: **Responder.** Hit back — rescue the comrades or make the brigade pay, loudly, so the price of a raid goes up. *(high risk; +poder or a bloodbath)*

@rd_aguantar
on-arrival: {! Q.u_celulas-=1; var _casc=(Q.u_seguridad < 45 + (Math.random()*30)); if(_casc){Q.u_celulas-=2;Q.u_calor+=6;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+2;Q.u_cascada=(Q.u_cascada||0)+1;}else{Q.u_seguridad+=2;} Q.u_calor-=6; if(Q.u_calor<0){Q.u_calor=0;} if(Q.u_celulas<0){Q.u_celulas=0;} if(Q.u_celulas<=0){Q.u_fin=1;Q.members=0;} !}

You do the hardest thing, which is nothing: you trust the seals and the silence of the taken. [? if u_seguridad >= 55 : The compartments hold. The interrogations yield names that lead to doors already abandoned, cells that were never told what they were not told. The Brigada Blanca has a cell and a dead end, and the network — bloodied by one door — survives, which in this war is the only victory there is. ?][? if u_seguridad < 55 : They were not sealed tightly enough. A name leads to an address leads to a name, and for three days you listen to the network come apart over the police radio, cell by cell, the cascade you built too loose to stop. This is how the Liga died. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

@rd_disolver
on-arrival: {! Q.u_celulas-=2; if(Q.u_celulas<0){Q.u_celulas=0;} Q.u_poder-=6; if(Q.u_poder<0){Q.u_poder=0;} Q.u_calor=20; Q.u_seguridad+=10; if(Q.u_seguridad>100){Q.u_seguridad=100;} if(Q.u_celulas<=0){Q.u_fin=1;Q.members=0;} !}

You assume the worst and act before the thread can pull: the order goes out to scatter, abandon every safehouse the taken cell could name, break contact, go completely to ground. It costs you — cells dissolved, the poder popular you were building set back, months of work walked away from. But the cascade dies for lack of anything left in place to catch, and the network survives in pieces that can be rewoven later. Guillén's cold wisdom: a movement that can vanish cannot be destroyed, only inconvenienced.

- @root: Continuar.

@rd_responder
on-arrival: {! var _r=(Q.u_celulas*7)+(Q.parque*0.4)-32+(Math.random()*36-14); if(_r>=0){Q.u_poder+=8;Q.legitimidad_regimen-=4;Q.u_celulas-=1;Q.apoyo_popular+=4;Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2;}else{Q.u_celulas-=3;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+3;Q.u_calor+=10;} Q.parque=(Q.parque||0)-6; if(Q.parque<0){Q.parque=0;} Q.u_calor+=8; if(Q.u_calor>100){Q.u_calor=100;} if(Q.u_celulas<0){Q.u_celulas=0;} if(Q.u_celulas<=0){Q.u_fin=1;Q.members=0;} !}

You refuse to only bleed. [? if u_celulas >= 3 : A commando hits the brigade where it did not expect to be hit — a rescue, or a reprisal that puts a price on the raid — and the city sees that the white brigade is not untouchable after all. The poder popular climbs; the state's aura of impunity cracks a little. It cost a cell and a great deal of nerve. ?][? if u_celulas < 3 : You did not have the strength for it, and it shows — the response is caught half-formed, comrades lost for a gesture, the brigade's price paid in your own blood instead of theirs. Courage is not a substitute for a network. ?] Either way the heat climbs, because nothing draws the state like being fought.

- @root: Continuar.
